From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Paint colour correctly on a CoreGraphics without linear
 colour spaces

The CoreGraphics of iOS 6 matches colour spaces by primaries and ignores
transfer functions, so it cannot hold a linear one. linearRGB becomes a
genuinely linear space the engine converts itself: pixels are converted
between sRGB and linearRGB when crossing pixel buffers, SVG filters interpolate
in linear light, a filter gets its source in the space this port paints in, and
linear sRGB stays distinguishable from sRGB. Gradients interpolate
premultiplied, paths are drawn through the native CoreGraphics sequence, and
the modern spelling of backdrop-filter reaches the style adjuster.
